
tar  --> won't compress

gzip  --> it compress

gunzip  --> it uncompress


=====================================

tar(archier)  --> files & folders: tapes all into one file, Preserving Linux file permissions and ownership,
-------------------------

tar -czvf test.tar.gz file/folder   --> to compress  (combination of gzip to make file smaller)
c → create archive
z → use gzip compression
v → verbose
f → filename


tar -xzvf test.tar.gz    --> to extract
x → extract
z → gzip
v → verbose
f → filename




gzip(compresser) --> files alone:
---------------------

gzip file1       --> it will remove the file1 and create zip
gzip -k file1    --> it will keep the file1 and create zip
gzip -r folder   --> it will zip all files in folder individually, we will find multiple zips for each file in that folder

gunzip file1.gz   --> to unzip





zip  --> multiple files:  -->  It compresses each file individually before putting them in the archive.
------------------------

zip myfiles.zip blog.txt file.txt    --> to zip
zip -r folder.zip folder        --> to zip folder
zip -re folder.zip folder      --> e-->encrypt, password protect
zip -re -P "password" folder.zip folder    --> in scripts



